I thought about bolt-on hacks for speed a couple months ago, and then
started digging into a way to just redo the speed system and split
"movement" and "attack" speeds up somehow.  There are some problems with
making monsters faster than speed 12 right now that are related to the
critter getting multiple attacks, even if you're roughly the same speed;
I tried several tweaks to locusts before having to finally just put them
at speed 12 for now, even though I want them to be speed 18 and constantly
next to the player.  The problem was that even while limiting sickness
attacks, it was still possible for one to get two turns and hit you with
Ill twice.  That's not a way I want to go.

(Pestilence can't do this because he's speed 12, for example; all the
Riders suffer from the same issue, they can't catch the player on Astral
and thus are far less scary than they should be.)

